          "op": "values-key",
          "path": "bpf.enableTCX",
          "state": "equals",
          "values": [
            "false"
          ]
        }
      },
      "consequence": {
        "kind": "behavior-change",
        "exposedClass": "review-required",
        "statement": "Cilium will attach tc BPF programs using tcx BPF links instead of old-style tc BPF attachment on Linux kernel 6.6+; if third-party old-style tc BPF users are present and bpf.enableTCX is not explicitly set to false, this behavioral switch may cause compatibility issues with those third-party tools."
      },
      "statement": "For Linux kernels 6.6 or newer, Cilium 1.16.0 defaults to tcx BPF links for tc BPF program attachment instead of old-style tc BPF attachment; environments with third-party old-style tc BPF users can disable this via Helm value bpf.enableTCX=false to maintain backward compatibility."
    },
